    {
      "rowData": {
        "widgetData": {
          "content": "<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">The Hatters&rsquo; third and final group-stage match in the English Football League/Jersey Mike&rsquo;s Trophy saw them make sure of finishing top of Northern Group E with a draw, followed by a victorious penalty shoot-out, at Edgeley Park against Tranmere.</span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">With the Hatters having already qualified for the Second Round, the questions remaining were whether they would do so as table-toppers (with a view to being seeded for a home-tie next month), and if the League Two visitors, by avoiding defeat, could also go through to the knockout phase with one further game left to play. </span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">As things turned out, both were achieved, as the fourth meeting between the two sides in the history of the competition ended scoreless - before a much-changed County team secured a bonus point to guarantee top spot in the group, as Luca Ashby-Hammond kept out two penalties, and Mamadou Jobe converted the fourth successful kick taken by the Hatters.</span></p>",
          "contentDouble": null,
          "imageKey": null,
          "mediaLibraryID": null,
          "toggleDouble": null
        },
        "widgetID": "e82d76f1-dd4d-11f1-87f8-931b2ad2afa4",
        "widgetName": "Text Block",
        "widgetType": "TextBlockWidget"
      },
      "rowID": "e82d76f0-dd4d-11f1-87f8-931b2ad2afa4"
    },
