    {
      "rowData": {
        "widgetData": {
          "content": "<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Shortly before the clock struck 7pm, the Hatters took to the field for an earlier-than-usual kick-off on a chilly, clear evening - and with a starting line-up showing nine changes from that in the FA Cup at Cray Wanderers two days earlier. The two survivors were Ashby-Hammond and Che Garner, whose minutes in the Cup-tie had been restricted to a little over 30 apiece due to the former&rsquo;s dismissal and the latter&rsquo;s consequential sacrifice for substitution.<span class=\"apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Eighteen-year-old central defender Dan Marshall, one of six teenagers handed a start, took his first-team bow for County - while the Hatters&rsquo; bench, like their initial 11, featured a good mix of further youth and more senior experience, including, in substitutes Lewis Bate, Ryan Glover and Jobe, three squad regulars who had not travelled to Cray.<span class=\"apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">The Tranmere starters, meanwhile, included a couple of players boasting full international experience, with goalkeeper Coniah Boyce-Clarke and skipper Lee O&rsquo;Connor having gained senior caps for Jamaica and the Republic of Ireland, respectively.</span></p>",
          "contentDouble": null,
          "imageKey": null,
          "mediaLibraryID": null,
          "toggleDouble": null
        },
        "widgetID": "a4555781-dd4e-11f1-9636-5182e7e8dc03",
        "widgetName": "Text Block",
        "widgetType": "TextBlockWidget"
      },
      "rowID": "a4555780-dd4e-11f1-9636-5182e7e8dc03"
    },
